  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving natural resources management through the integration of the civil society, DRC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is an Internal grant from Cafod General Fund to support activities related to the project titled &quot;improving natural resources management through the integration of Civil Society in DR Congo&quot;. The project&apos;s duration is for three years (from February 2011 to February 2014). The CAFOD Advocacy Support Programme Officer will conduct these activities in supporting the partner CERN as well as activities implemented on the ground by Civil Society Platform called &quot;Cadre de Concertation&quot; (CdC) and those covered by 6 Observatories of Natural Resources (ORN in acronym) especially in Mbandaka, Inongo, Bunia, Beni Butembo, Kalemi and Kananga in the Dem.Rep. of Congo. 
By this grant CAFOD and CERN intend to:
- Contribute in supporting natural resources management programme in DR Congo  in light to establish and to strengthen the Congolese&#x2019;s Civil society on natural resources issues,
- Increase understanding of issues by local people relating to the management of Natural resources and their rights recognized in this matter.
- Facilitate involvement of the Congolese Civil Society Organizations on the decision making process and on influencing politics about the natural resources management.
Finally this grant will support and focused in supporting advocacy work and initiative undertaken by the partner as well as CdC, ORN, CSOs with regular and sufficient support from the CAFOD/Advocacy Support Programme Officer.</narrative>
  </description>
